WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.320
- As always, lets finish
up with a little good news

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.776
trending on social,
this is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.776 --> 00:00:07.320
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.840
For decades, Sister Libby
worked with the Sacramento

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.220
non-profit supporting the
unhoused in her community.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.026
Then, five years ago, she
had an even bigger idea.

00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:16.809
Instead of helping from a building,

00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:19.452
why not go to the people
directly on the streets.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.997
Since then, she's built
up an army of volunteers

00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:24.420
and they're easy to spot on any given day,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.198
because they show up on bicycles.

00:00:26.198 --> 00:00:28.076
They call it, "Mercy Peddling."

00:00:28.076 --> 00:00:30.390
To tell us more about it, let's say hello

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.130
to Sister Libby, everybody.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.299
Hello!

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.572
- Hello, Kelly.

00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:36.940
- Hello, that is a really cool bike.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.940
I'm gonna lead with that, first of all.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.572
But, tell us more about how you help.

00:00:40.572 --> 00:00:42.684
- Well, first of all,
I'm a Sister of Mercy

00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:46.314
for over 32 years, and I was inspired

00:00:46.314 --> 00:00:49.120
by the sisters actually
doing the works of mercy,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.019
going out in the streets
and doing Matthew 25.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:57.100
Especially, "When I was
homeless, you gave me shelter."

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:57.933
- Yeah.

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.980
- So, we Mercy Peddlers use these trikes

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.440
and we go out in different neighborhoods

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.660
connecting with those
who are on the streets,

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.496
and we bring water, and nutritional bars,

00:01:07.496 --> 00:01:11.949
hygiene items, soap,
shampoo, and a lot of love.

00:01:11.949 --> 00:01:13.180
- Aw, I love that.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.236
So, you offer more than
just food and supplies

00:01:15.236 --> 00:01:16.092
though, right?

00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:18.150
- Oh, absolutely.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.520
Our ministry is really based
on a sense of presence,

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.800
dignity and respect.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.800
So, over time we grow
in a mutual relationship

00:01:28.856 --> 00:01:33.116
of trust and care, so then we
can ask the deeper questions.

00:01:33.116 --> 00:01:36.097
"How can I receive shelter today?"

00:01:36.097 --> 00:01:37.272
"Do you need housing?"

00:01:37.272 --> 00:01:39.607
"Do you have any recovery programs?"

00:01:39.607 --> 00:01:41.434
"What about mental health services?"

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.369
So, we get to those deeper questions

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.808
and then we connect with
other community organizations

00:01:46.808 --> 00:01:49.492
to help them make that major, major step

00:01:49.492 --> 00:01:50.929
off of the streets.

00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:53.010
- Absolutely, which is the whole point.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.396
Thank you so much, Sister Libby.

00:01:54.396 --> 00:01:55.997
You've got such a great heart.

00:01:55.997 --> 00:01:58.233
I'm liking your post right now, alright?

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:00.634
And, that's not all.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.190
That's not all, ma'am.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:03.840
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.126
makers of G2, the go to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.868
want to celebrate people like you,

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:10.650
making a big impact in their community.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.560
So, they are giving Mercy
Peddlers a thousand dollars,

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.397
how's that sound?

00:02:14.397 --> 00:02:15.766
(audience cheering)

00:02:15.766 --> 00:02:17.670
- That is so great.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.680
Your care is gonna really touch those

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.610
who are on the streets.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.720
God bless you.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.590
- [Kelly] Aw, God bless you, too.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.436
Thank you so much, and thank
you to all of our guests

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:28.243
this hour, Meghan Trainor,
Dara Selvara, Tom Colfree,

00:02:28.243 --> 00:02:30.990
Jeremy Ford and Lawrence
Erin, y'all have a great day,

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.740
and if it's not, try and change it.

